---
const levers = [
  "Giving a damn",
  "Code review",
  "Manual testing",
  "Unit tests",
  "Integration tests",
  "End-to-end tests",
  "Property testing",
  "Fuzzing",
  "Formal QA",
  "Dogfooding",
  "Demos",
  "Observability",
  "Specification design",
];
const models = [
  {
    name: "Typical process",
    rate: "6.33",
    coding: 80,
    enabled: [0, 1, 2, 3, 11],
  },
  {
    name: "Layered process",
    rate: "3.75",
    coding: 50,
    enabled: [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 11],
  },
];
---

<quality-layers
  class="not-prose my-12 block border-y border-border bg-surface-raised/40 py-6 sm:py-8"
>
  <header class="mb-6">
    <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-text-heading">
      Defect rates by quality process
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-text-secondary">
      Defects that slip through, per 100 possible defects. Lower is better.
      Change either process to compare.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div
    class="sticky top-28 min-[52.01rem]:top-20 z-10 bg-surface py-3"
    data-chart
  >
    <div
      class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 sm:gap-8"
      aria-label="Remaining defects comparison"
    >
      {
        models.map((model, side) => (
          <div class="min-w-0 text-center">
            <p class="text-xs text-text-secondary">{model.name}</p>
            <p
              class="my-2 font-serif text-3xl tabular-nums text-text-heading"
              data-result
            >
              {model.rate}%
            </p>
            <div
              class="relative flex h-24 sm:h-40 items-end justify-center border-y border-border bg-surface-overlay/40"
              aria-hidden="true"
            >
              <div class="absolute inset-x-0 top-1/2 border-t border-dashed border-border" />
              <div
                data-bar
                class:list={[
                  "relative w-2/5",
                  side === 0 ? "bg-text-secondary" : "bg-accent",
                ]}
                style={`height: ${Number(model.rate) * 10}%`}
              />
            </div>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
    <p
      class="mt-3 text-xs text-text-secondary"
      data-comparison
      aria-live="polite"
      aria-atomic="true"
    >
      Typical: 6.33%. Layered: 3.75%. Layered has 40.7% fewer escaping defects.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-text-secondary" data-scale>
      Shared scale: 0–10% · adjusts with your inputs
    </p>
  </div>

  <form class="mt-6">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 sm:gap-8">
      {
        models.map((model) => (
          <fieldset disabled data-model class="min-w-0">
            <legend class="mb-2 text-sm font-semibold text-text-heading">
              {model.name}
            </legend>
            {levers.map((name, index) => (
              <div data-lever class="scroll-mt-96 border-t border-border py-3">
                <label class="flex min-h-11 cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-2 text-xs leading-snug sm:text-sm">
                  <span>{name}</span>
                  <input
                    type="checkbox"
                    role="switch"
                    checked={model.enabled.includes(index)}
                    aria-label={`${model.name}: ${name}`}
                    class="quality-switch"
                  />
                </label>
                <div class="mt-2 flex items-center gap-2">
                  <input
                    type="range"
                    min="0"
                    max="100"
                    step="1"
                    value={index === 0 ? model.coding : 25}
                    disabled={!model.enabled.includes(index)}
                    aria-label={`${model.name}: ${name} effectiveness`}
                    class="min-h-6 w-full min-w-0 accent-accent disabled:opacity-30"
                  />
                  <output class="w-10 shrink-0 text-right text-xs tabular-nums text-text-secondary">
                    {index === 0 ? model.coding : 25}%
                  </output>
                </div>
              </div>
            ))}
          </fieldset>
        ))
      }
    </div>
    <button
      type="reset"
      disabled
      class="mt-5 min-h-11 border border-border px-4 text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-text-primary hover:border-border-hover disabled:opacity-40"
      >Reset to article defaults</button
    >
  </form>
  <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-text-secondary" data-status role="status">
    Loading the Rust/WASM calculator…
  </p>
  <noscript
    ><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-text-secondary">
      Enable JavaScript to adjust the model. The bars show the article’s
      defaults.
    </p></noscript
  >
  <details class="mt-4 text-xs leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
    <summary class="cursor-pointer py-2 text-text-primary"
      >How the model works</summary
    >
    <p class="mt-2">
      Each enabled layer removes its effectiveness percentage of the defects
      still remaining, not of the original total. Remaining defects = 100 × the
      product of (1 − effectiveness / 100). These are illustrative assumptions,
      not measured guarantees; real safeguards can share blind spots.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2">
      Typical: 80% from coding, then four layers at 25%. Layered: 50% from
      coding, then nine layers at 25%. The article does not name those nine;
      here they are review, manual, unit, integration, end-to-end, property
      testing, fuzzing, QA, and observability. All other layers start off.
    </p>
  </details>
</quality-layers>

<script>
  import "../scripts/quality-layers.js";
</script>
